1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,910
What was wrong with the man's story?
这个人的说法有什么问题？

2
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:16,540
What was wrong with the man's story?
这个人的说法有什么问题？

3
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:27,200
'At the time the murder was committed I was travelling on the 8 o'clock train to London,' said the man.
“凶杀发生时，我正坐在8点钟开往伦敦的火车上，”那人说。

4
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:33,670
'Do you always catch such an early train?' asked the inspector.
“你总是赶这么早的火车吗？”探长问。

5
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:38,050
'Of course I do,' answered the man.
“当然，”那人回答说。

6
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:41,100
'I must be at work at 10 o'clock.
“我必须在10点钟上班。

7
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:45,800
My employer will confirm that I was there on time.'
我的雇主会证实我是准时到的。”

8
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:53,490
'Would a later train get you to work on time?' asked the inspector.
“坐晚一点的火车也能准时上班吗？”探长问。

9
00:00:55,270 --> 00:00:59,580
'I suppose it would, but I never catch a later train.'
“我想可以，不过我从来不坐晚一点的车。”

10
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:04,990
'At what time did you arrive at the station?'
“你是什么时候到车站的？”

11
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:12,150
'At ten to eight. I bought a paper and waited for the train.'
“八点差十分。我买了份报纸，然后等车。”

12
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:18,070
'And you didn't notice anything unusual?'
“你没有注意到什么异常情况吗？”

13
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:22,720
'Of course not.'
“当然没有。”

14
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:28,170
'I suggest,' said the inspector,' that you are not telling the truth.
“我认为，”探长说，“你讲的不是实话。

15
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:33,500
I suggest that you did not catch the 8 o'clock train,
我认为你没赶上8点钟的火车，

16
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:39,700
but that you caught the 8.25 which would still get you to work on time.
而是赶上了8点25分的车，坐那趟车照样能准时上班。

17
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:47,550
You see, on the morning of the murder, the 8 o'clock train did not run at all.
你要知道，凶杀发生的那天早上，8点钟的火车根本没开。

18
00:01:47,570 --> 00:01:53,390
It broke down at Ferngreen station and was taken off the line.'
它在芬格林车站出了故障，被取消了。”
